You found an early amulet of life saving, which you had to use up (so it 
was *very* useful), you found a bag of holding, a luckstone, an early 
shield of reflection *and* early gauntlets of power, and you're 
complaining about startingly bad luck?

< Scratches his head... >

> My grand plan is SDSM and cloak of MR, with Mojo and a silver saber.
> I have none of those currently.  I feel unlucky (in RL, again), and
> have my doubts about making it to that wonderful wand in the castle.

> Do I burn this first wish on:
> SDSM, though I already have means of reflection?

Definitely not. SDSM is useful for spellcasters, since they cannot use 
shields when they want to be effective. Non-spellcasters should go for 
GDSM for the MR, which is invaluable. DSM also provides a nice AC boost, 
which you seem worried about.

> Cloak of MR, though it won't help my AC as much?

Never mind your AC. At the dungeon levels you're on, MR is at least as 
important, since there are polymorph traps.

> Speed boots?

Always a good idea; it'll also help in your AC (which, by the way, isn't 
so bad at all.

> Mojo, because I haven't found a lawful altar?  (Probably the worst
> idea of the bunch!)

Indeed. I'll come sooner or later. The same goes for an amulet of 
reflection. Once you find one of those, you may consider dropping your 
shield and starting twoweaponing.

